{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"15215","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/15215","key":"MC-189837","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"15/Jun/20 7:48 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p><b>What I expected to happen:</b></p>\n\n<p>When I logged on to a Minecraft world that was thunder storming in the Overworld, I went into the Nether and expected the fog to be the normal color.</p>\n\n<p><b>What actually happened:</b></p>\n\n<p>The Nether fog was a lot darker than usual</p>\n\n<p><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create a new world</li>\n\t<li>Set the weather to rain and thunder<span class=\"#172b4d\"> (</span><tt><span class=\"#505f79\">/weather thunder</span><span class=\"#172b4d\">)</span></tt></li>\n\t<li>Go into the nether</li>\n\t<li>Quit the world and enter it again</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p>The nether fog appears a lot darker. This will stay like this until it stops raining in the overworld and you quit and re-enter the world again.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"15/Jun/20 4:54 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/24299","id":"24299","filename":"2020-12-03_10.03.48.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/48","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/24","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-